@host = http://localhost:5299
@gameId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### Health: the schema state
GET {{host}}/health

### 1. Create a heads-up game (201, ETag "1", Location header)
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games
Content-Type: application/json

{ "gameId": "{{gameId}}", "options": { "maxPlayersCount": 2 } }

### 2. Start it: two seats of 100, hand 1 is dealt (ETag "2")
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "joinSeats": [ { "name": "Alice", "seatNo": 1, "buyInAmount": 100 }, { "name": "Bob", "seatNo": 2, "buyInAmount": 100 } ] }

### 3. Read it back (the ETag does not change)
GET {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}

### 4. Act: the small blind calls (ETag "3")
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "2"

{ "actionType": "Call" }

### 5. A stale If-Match: the game is at version 3, so this is 412 with code "Conflict"
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "2"

{ "actionType": "Check" }

### 6. Keep playing until the hand ends (Check or Call, as handData.evaluations offers), then deal the next hand
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "actionType": "Check" }

### 7. The next hand (409 PreviousHandNotEnded until the current one has ended)
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}/hands

### 8. Finish the game (between hands only)
POST {{host}}/api/holdem/games/{{gameId}}/finish
